## Reviewer points not followed

- sv-a 30 and sv-b 6. A space as the thousands separator is normal Swedish. The checker does not parse it for `sv`, and ACCEPTED-ROUND says to skip it. Period thousands stay.
- sv-a 14 and sv-b 10. The U+200B lines match the Korean source. Promoting Q16–Q20 would also change heading levels. They are not disposable blank lines.
- sv-a 2. The opened page is article 3, and the withholding label is already the right description of that link. Korean 영업세법 제10조 is still counted, so "(artikel 10)" stays. The URL was not changed.
- sv-a 16. "ett" in "per ett år" carries the digit 1. It is not a spare word next to *per*.
- sv-a 17, in part. "per skadad person och per olycka" is the better Swedish. It deletes two digits the checker counts. "per 1 … och per 1 …" keeps both the preposition and the digits.
- sv-a 4, in part. "I praxis utdöms i regel" restores the typical-outcome sentence R3 replaced. *Fängelse* was added. The denial that there is no typical or guaranteed outcome stays.
- sv-a 24, in part. "garanterad synlighet" is the right denial, and the pack test bans that substring. The denial was rewritten without it.
- *Ställföreträdarskap* is a real Swedish legal noun. The flagged "legal ställföreträdarskap" in 007 was still rewritten to "rättsligt företrädande av barnet", because the English adjective made the list item unclear. 016 "lagligt ställföreträdarskap" was not swept; part b did not flag it.

